      "writtenOn": "2022-02-07T16:03:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The table isn\u0027t well formed, but it\u0027s redundant with the actual Kconfig.  As discussed in the last meeting, I think you should just create a single link to the Kconfig.usbc file.\n\nBecause there are so many configs, I think we should start splitting Kconfig.usbc into multiple files.\n\nSome potential sub-sections:\n* AP Boot power requirements\n* Retimers\n* TCPCs\n* PPCs\n* All the suboptions nested under PLATFORM_EC_USB_POWER_DELIVERY\n* FRS support\n* USB muxes\n\nThis doc can then just create links to each of the files.  Something like:\n\n\"The main USB-C Kconfig options are defined and documented in Kconfig.usbc.  To enable USB Power Delivery see Kconfig.usbpd.\n\nIf your board uses one more TCPCs, see Kconfig.tcpc.\"",
